{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791563212,"nonce":"Hw5Dd7no6uEuCKZ2bwCF0j2TtCE=","title":"Move ashui's CSS cascade onto blinc_abi's shared CSS engine","message":"blinc_abi 449ad475c22dc1ac91c9a0c9b212e2d9c0ef201552d0113575714b6fcedadc78 puts CSS parsing, selector matching, cascade and a compiled sheet format in blinc_abi, for every SDK (decided 2026-10-09). ashui's own engine (haxe/ashui/css, about 6,400 lines) stays until that one matches it.\n\n**Then**\n- CompiledCss keeps its compile-time advantage through the shared compiler: the macro runs blinc_abi's CSS command-line tool with sys.io.Process, reports its diagnostics as compile errors and warnings at their line in the .css file, and embeds the compiled sheet with Context.addResource; at run time the bytes go to native without parsing. The tool ships prebuilt with the haxelib.\n- Css.load and live reload parse through the native engine; restyle is native and incremental.\n- The Haxe API (Css, Stylesheet, Tw, themes) stays; underneath it, the Haxe parser and cascade go.\n- Check: the CSS tests and every pixel probe pass unchanged, and startup and restyle are no slower.","files":null}]}